    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0805" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg791"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish, Secretary of State, to Mr. Boutwell, Secretary
                        of the Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1860-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 24,
                        1860</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your letter of to day,
                    representing that a vessel is fitting out in Philadelphia for the revolutionists
                    in Cuba, and that two men, claiming to have been enlisted for that service,
                    offer information if paid therefor.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have to state that this Department will cause a reasonable sum to be
                    paid for the information referred to.</p>
                <p><seg type="margin">[67]</seg> *A copy of your letter has been sent to the
                    Attorney-General. I am, dear sir, yours, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">George S. Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
